<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Ochs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1752–1821</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Ochs was a Basel politician and historian who drafted the constitution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a>, imposed under French influence in 1798. Closely tied to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-directory">French Directory</a>, he sat in the republic's executive Directory until he was forced out in 1799. He later held office in the canton of Basel and wrote a history of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-ochs.jpg" alt="Peter Ochs" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, upload by sidonius 10:31, 15 December 2006 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Ochs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
